My father comes to the screen.
I ask, "Dad, where is your tea?"
Father smiles.
"Maya, who is your new friend in Kochi?" father asks.
I take my hot tea.
I walk to the desk.
I put the phone on the desk.
"My friend is Anitha," I say.
"She is a very good friend."
"She is my neighbor."
"Her home is in this building."
"She is a good guide for me."
"She helps me in this new city."
Father smiles again.
"Is she from Kochi?" he asks.
"Yes, she is a Kochi local," I say.
My father is very happy now.
